> Volunteers are vital to Thames Reach in our efforts to end street homelessness and support vulnerable and socially excluded people across London.
As well[ as] helping individuals to take steps forward in their lives, volunteering also offers opportunities to learn, meet[ new] people and experience something[ different].
Benefact[o is a] social enterprise helping to get people who work in a professional capacity to volunteer in their local communities. Since last June, they’ve been arranging for professional and corporate volunteers to dedicate some of their time to helping Thames[ Reach] clients at iRe[ach],[ a] weekly digital skills workshop at our Employment Academy in Camberwell.
iRe[ach gives] people with little or no computer skills the opportunity to learn at their own pace. Fund[ed by] the Worshipful Company of Information Techn[ologists], the workshop teaches practical digital skills, so clients can access[ services] and[ benefits] online, and can also help to reduce social isolation[.]
